# Go conventions

- Standard `gofmt`. Run `go vet ./...` from `agent/` before committing.
- Errors are values. Wrap with `fmt.Errorf("context: %w", err)` — no
  `errors.Wrap`.
- Concurrency: channels over shared state. Every goroutine has a clear
  termination story (context cancellation or channel close).
- All logs go to stderr (`log.SetOutput(os.Stderr)` is set in main.go).
  Never `fmt.Print*` to stdout — it corrupts the JSON-RPC stream.
- The agent loop (`internal/loop/`) must not import the Anthropic SDK
  directly. SDK types live in `internal/llm/`.

## Package layout

- `cmd/agent/` — entry point only, no business logic
- `internal/rpc/` — JSON-RPC codec
- `internal/loop/` — agent loop and tool dispatch
- `internal/llm/` — LLM client wrapper (SDK isolation)
- `internal/tools/` — tool registry and Go-side executors

When adding functionality, place it in the smallest package that owns it.
Do not create new top-level packages without updating `CLAUDE.md`.

## Cross-platform

- Always use `filepath.Join`, never string concatenation
- Use `runtime.GOOS` only for behavioral branching, never for paths
- File modes: `0o644` for files, `0o755` for executables
